<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ApprovalProcess xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <ApprovalProcess> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error. The rationale below lives in this comment
        rather than in <description> because a comment is repo-only and is never sent to the
        Metadata API. ⚠ DO NOT ASSUME THE 255-CHARACTER CAP that binds RecordType and
        ValidationRule descriptions applies here: the five approval files already in this repo
        carry descriptions of 442 to 617 characters (measured against git HEAD, 2026-08-19).
        The descriptions written in this change are nevertheless kept under 255, so the rule is
        uniform across every metadata type in this tranche and never has to be re-measured.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 2026-08-19: THIS FILE NOW DOES THE EXACT THING DESIGN DECISION Q4 FORBADE, AND THE
        SUPERSEDING ARGUMENT IS RECORDED HERE SO NOBODY RESTORES Q4 FROM ITS OWN REASONING.
        =====================================================================================
        Q4's decision is quoted verbatim from Wire_Complete_Before_Completed's XML comment, and
        it is RETRACTED:

            RETRACTED: "WHY THIS SHAPE, NOT AN APPROVAL entryCriteria (design Q4): Putting the
            flag in Closing_Approval's entryCriteria would surface an unmet gate as the
            platform's 'no applicable approval process was found' - a misleading error the user
            cannot act on. Instead the flag is an approvalPageFields entry on Closing_Approval so
            the approver SEES the wire state when deciding, and the hard stop lives [in the
            validation rule] where its message renders natively in the Path UI."

        WHY IT DIED - THE PREMISE, NOT THE PRINCIPLE. Q4 was right that an unmet gate must not
        surface as the platform's unhelpful message. Its premise was that entry criteria are the
        ONLY place the user would meet that gate. Two things changed:
          1. THE MITIGATION NOW EXISTS. Submission no longer happens through the platform's
             generic Submit button. It happens through the Submit_Closing_Approval quick action,
             backed by DispositionApprovalService.submitForApproval, which PRE-CHECKS
             Wire_Verification_Completed__c and raises an AUTHORED message naming the six wire
             confirmation fields. The user never reaches the platform's message. That authored
             pre-check is the load-bearing half of this change; if it is ever removed, this entry
             criterion must be removed with it or Q4's failure mode returns.
          2. WITHOUT THE CRITERION THERE IS NOW A DEADLOCK, WHICH DID NOT EXIST UNDER Q4.
             recordEditability = AdminOnly locks the Disposition while the approval is pending,
             so Wire_Verification_Rollup cannot write Wire_Verification_Completed__c during that
             window - it fails soft. Under Q4 that only cost a signposting sentence on the Path,
             because a human moved the stage afterwards and could simply wait. Now the APPROVAL
             owns the stage move: approve with the wire unverified and the semaphore fires, the
             Queueable writes Sale Closes, and the wire validation rule REFUSES it - leaving the
             deal approved, unadvanced and the flag stuck true. Requiring the wire BEFORE entry
             removes the window entirely.

        🔴 THE VALIDATION RULE IS NOT REPLACED BY THIS - BOTH GATES STAY, AND THEY GUARD
        DIFFERENT THINGS. Wire_Complete_Before_Sale_Closes still blocks any write of
        'Sale Closes', including the Queueable's, including a hand edit that never went near an
        approval. This criterion only decides who may ENTER the approval. Do not delete either
        on the grounds that the other exists.

        🔴 IT NOW CARRIES A FINAL APPROVAL ACTION, AND IT IS A SEMAPHORE, NOT A STAGE WRITE.
        Retracted from this file's own previous description: "No field updates fire on approval
        or rejection - one would bypass that validation rule entirely." The objection is answered
        rather than ignored: Set_Approval_Advance_Pending writes a FLAG, which re-fires
        DispositionTrigger, which enqueues DispositionApprovalAdvanceQueueable, which writes the
        stage with ordinary Database.update(..., false, AccessLevel.SYSTEM_MODE). Validation
        rules DO evaluate against that write - which is exactly why the deadlock in point 2 was
        real and had to be closed here.

        ⚠ ONE RESIDUAL, ACCEPTED AND FAIL-CLOSED. If the wire flag flips back to FALSE between
        submission and the Queueable running (an admin unticking a verbal verification after the
        approval resolves), the validation rule refuses the advance and the semaphore is LEFT
        TRUE. Visible by SOQL on Approval_Advance_Pending__c, recoverable, and preferable to a
        silent skip.

        Wire_Verification_Completed__c STAYS in approvalPageFields as well. Under Q4 that was
        the whole mitigation; it is now redundant for gating but still the right thing to show
        an approver, and removing it would cost information for no gain.

        DEPLOY ORDER - LOAD-BEARING. workflows/Disposition__c.workflow-meta.xml must land FIRST.

        =====================================================================================
        2026-08-21 - THREE NEW ELEMENTS, PLUS A SECOND ACTION ON finalApprovalActions.
        =====================================================================================
        initialSubmissionActions (new) sets Disposition__c.Approval_Pending__c;
        finalApprovalActions gains Clear_Approval_Pending as a SECOND action;
        finalRejectionActions (new, this file had none) and recallActions (new) clear it.
        Set_Approval_Advance_Pending is untouched and stays FIRST. Purpose: hide the
        Submit_Closing_Approval quick action on Disposition_Record_Page while this approval is
        genuinely pending.

        🔴 THE FULL ARGUMENT, THE EVIDENCE FOR THE TWO PREVIOUSLY UNPROVEN ELEMENT SHAPES, AND
        THE MANDATORY SUBMIT-THEN-RECALL READBACK LIVE IN ONE PLACE AND ARE NOT REPEATED HERE:
        approvalProcesses/Disposition__c.Sale_Decision_Approval.approvalProcess-meta.xml,
        2026-08-21 entry. That file is deliberately deployed and behaviourally proven FIRST AND
        ALONE. Do not deploy this file until its recall test has passed.

        ⚠ THIS PROCESS HAS THE MOST TO LOSE FROM A recallActions BLOCK THAT DEPLOYS BUT DOES NOT
        FIRE, AND THE REASON IS TWO PARAGRAPHS UP. The entry criterion above requires
        Wire_Verification_Completed__c, and the AdminOnly lock already stops
        Wire_Verification_Rollup writing that field during the pending window. Add a Submit
        button hidden by a flag that never clears and a recalled Closing deal has NO route
        forward at all: the button is gone, the wire flag cannot be recomputed by resubmitting,
        and the record sits at Closing indefinitely. That is why the readback is mandatory and
        why this file waits for it.

        ⚠ THE RESIDUAL ALREADY RECORDED ABOVE IS NOT MADE WORSE BY THIS. If the wire flag flips
        false between submission and the Queueable running, Approval_Advance_Pending__c is left
        TRUE while Approval_Pending__c is correctly FALSE, so the Submit button REAPPEARS and the
        stuck record stays actionable. Fail open, and identical to today's behaviour.

        ⚠ Approval_Pending__c AND Approval_Advance_Pending__c ARE OPPOSITES IN TIME AND ARE NOT
        INTERCHANGEABLE. Read the banner on
        objects/Disposition__c/fields/Approval_Pending__c.field-meta.xml first.

        =====================================================================================
        2026-08-26 - LABEL RENAME ONLY. Process <label> stays "Closing Approval" (already
        distinct); step <label> changed from "Principal Review" to "Principal approves closing".
        All five disposition approvals previously carried the step label "Principal Review", so
        approvers saw identical names on every approval request and could not tell which decision
        they were being asked for. fullName / developer name (Disposition__c.Closing_Approval)
        and step <name> (Principal_Review_Step) are UNCHANGED. Zero runtime impact:
        DispositionApprovalService.submit calls Approval.process(request) with only setObjectId
        set, auto-routed by entryCriteria alone, never by name or label - confirmed by grep
        across force-app/main/default/classes, which found no setProcessDefinitionNameOrId call
        anywhere in the repo.
        =====================================================================================
    -->
    <active>true</active>
    <allowRecall>true</allowRecall>
    <allowedSubmitters>
        <type>owner</type>
    </allowedSubmitters>
    <approvalPageFields>
        <field>Name</field>
        <field>Owner</field>
        <field>Disposition_Stage__c</field>
        <field>PSA_Executed__c</field>
        <field>Title_Company__c</field>
        <field>Accepted_Offer_Price__c</field>
        <field>Net_Sale_Proceeds__c</field>
        <field>Wire_Verification_Completed__c</field>
    </approvalPageFields>
    <approvalStep>
        <allowDelegate>false</allowDelegate>
        <assignedApprover>
            <approver>
                <name>nikhil.dhanani@usmandpeg.uat</name>
                <type>user</type>
            </approver>
            <approver>
                <name>aftab.ali.dpeg.usman@avanzasolutions.com</name>
                <type>user</type>
            </approver>
            <whenMultipleApprovers>FirstResponse</whenMultipleApprovers>
        </assignedApprover>
        <label>Principal approves closing</label>
        <name>Principal_Review_Step</name>
    </approvalStep>
    <description>Principal decision to approve the final sale terms and closing wire. Entry: stage is Closing AND Wire Verification Completed is true. Approval fires the Set_Approval_Advance_Pending semaphore; a Queueable then advances the stage to Sale Closes.</description>
    <enableMobileDeviceAccess>false</enableMobileDeviceAccess>
    <entryCriteria>
        <booleanFilter>1 AND 2</booleanFilter>
        <criteriaItems>
            <field>Disposition__c.Disposition_Stage__c</field>
            <operation>equals</operation>
            <value>Closing</value>
        </criteriaItems>
        <criteriaItems>
            <field>Disposition__c.Wire_Verification_Completed__c</field>
            <operation>equals</operation>
            <value>True</value>
        </criteriaItems>
    </entryCriteria>
    <finalApprovalActions>
        <action>
            <name>Set_Approval_Advance_Pending</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
        <action>
            <name>Clear_Approval_Pending</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
    </finalApprovalActions>
    <finalApprovalRecordLock>false</finalApprovalRecordLock>
    <finalRejectionActions>
        <action>
            <name>Clear_Approval_Pending</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
    </finalRejectionActions>
    <finalRejectionRecordLock>false</finalRejectionRecordLock>
    <initialSubmissionActions>
        <action>
            <name>Set_Approval_Pending</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
    </initialSubmissionActions>
    <label>Closing Approval</label>
    <processOrder>3</processOrder>
    <recallActions>
        <action>
            <name>Clear_Approval_Pending</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
    </recallActions>
    <recordEditability>AdminOnly</recordEditability>
    <showApprovalHistory>true</showApprovalHistory>
</ApprovalProcess>
